WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.909
Speaker 1: Donald Trump faces 33 years in
prison.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:10.280
For just what the DOJ is investigating him
for, as well as the loss of his ability to

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.570
hold public office.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:17.020
That is the maximum possible penalty for Donald
Trump based on what he is being investigated

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.150
for.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.970
There are basically three elements to this,
and we're going to look at each of them.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.270
You've got the Espionage Act.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:29.410
If Trump is found guilty of violating the
Espionage Act, he would pay face fines and

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.350
up to ten years in prison.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:38.370
Now, the search warrant from Friday cites
18 U.S. Code 793.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.739
That's a part of the Espionage Act, which
refers to the, quote, gathering, transmitting

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:46.989
or losing defense information.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:47.989
Some of the stock.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:50.670
The documents reportedly relate to nuclear
weapons.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:56.700
So if charged for that violation, Trump could
be looking at fines and up to ten years in

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.840
prison.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.690
Part two of this investigation in connection
with the FBI's search warrant served at Mar

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:06.840
a Lago is concealment of documents there.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.509
We are looking at possible fines and up to
three years in prison.

00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:14.700
The warrant points to 18 U.S. Code 2071.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.549
That's on the, quote, concealment, removal
or mutilation generally.

00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:24.320
And based on that provision, it is illegal
to take government documents.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.740
It makes it a crime for anyone to have any
federal record in their possession with the

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.329
intent to either conceal or destroy.

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:37.359
So if charged there, if convicted, trumps
looking at a fine or three years in prison.

00:01:37.359 --> 00:01:41.819
But very importantly and this is why 2071
has been a big deal over the last few days.

00:01:41.819 --> 00:01:45.929
If Trump is found guilty there, he could be
disqualified from holding any public office

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:46.929
in the future.

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:49.130
Could be very relevant in 2024.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:54.710
And then the third element here is obstruction
of justice, possible fines, and up to 20 years

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:55.710
in prison.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.139
Admittedly, most people don't get 20 years
for obstruction of justice, but that would

00:01:59.139 --> 00:02:06.490
be 18 U.S. Code 1519 that deals with the,
quote, destruction, alteration or falsification

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:10.709
of records in federal investigations and bankruptcy.

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:15.790
You are also forbidden from destroying federal
records, and this is the highest potential

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.569
sentence, the 20 year sentence and fines are
relatively modest.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:26.310
Now, we are many, many steps from anybody
talking about prison time, but this is if

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:31.930
we're if the question is being asked, what
is the most that we could be looking at for

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:34.220
what the DOJ is investigating?

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.000
Remember, there's the Georgia investigation.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.000
There's all these other things.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Forget about that.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.900
Just for what DOJ is investigating.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:47.329
If Trump was found guilty in all three of
these areas, if he got the stiffest sentence,

00:02:47.329 --> 00:02:53.370
and if the sentences ran consecutively rather
than concurrently, you could be looking at

00:02:53.370 --> 00:03:00.790
33 years fines and loss of ability disqualification
from holding public office.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:03.560
Is it likely that we would ever get to that?

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.829
The answer is no, but the next step would
be indictment.

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:14.170
Then you would have a trial slash plea if
you get guilty verdicts.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.400
Then you have sentencing appeals.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.920
So this is a very, very long road.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:25.670
But at the end of this path, the absolute
maximum would be that the 33 years fines can't

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.260
run for public office.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:33.920
If you believe Trump will ever see anything
like that or even a day behind prison bars,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.670
let me know.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.739
I still don't see it.

